course: dictionary
lesson: 9694
title: One word, many meanings
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words have more than one meaning, and the context tells you which one is meant. The word sugar is a good example. «The crushed cane stems left over are burned to power the sugar mills.» Here sugar is the sweet food made into grains, because a sugar mill makes it.
explain: Sugar can also be a fond name for someone you love, like «honey». Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about a person talking to someone, the word is probably a name, not a food.
explain: Sugar can also be a verb, meaning to add sugar to something. Try your meaning in the sentence instead of the word. If «add sugar to» still makes sense, you have found the right meaning.
fact: Sugar is a sweet food, made into white or brown grains, and used in cakes and drinks.
fact: Sugar comes from sugar cane or sugar beet.
fact: «Sugar» can also be a fond name for someone, like «honey».
fact: Sugars are sweet substances in food, like those in fruit and milk.
fact: «A lollipop is sugar syrup boiled until almost all the water is gone, so it sets hard and glassy.»
exercise: «The crushed cane stems left over are burned to power the sugar mills.» What does sugar mean here? | To add sweetness to a drink | A kind of fruit | *A sweet food made into grains | A fond name for a friend
exercise: Mum calls Sam «sugar». What does she mean? | A sweet fruit from the shop | *A fond name, like honey | A bag of white grains for cakes | A cup of tea
exercise: What word means sweet substances, like those in fruit and milk? | sugar-free | *sugars | icing sugar | sugar cane
test: «Connor looks both up: a toque is a woolly hat, a double-double is coffee with two creams and two sugars.» What are the sugars in this sentence? | A woolly hat | Sweet fruit | Two creams | *Spoonfuls of sweet stuff added to the coffee
test: Which sentence uses sugar as a verb, meaning to add sugar? | *Grandma sugars the strawberries before she adds the cream | Sugar is sold in white bags at the shop | The sugar cane stems are burned to power the mills
exam: «A lollipop is sugar syrup boiled until almost all the water is gone.» What does sugar mean in this sentence? | A sugar glider that glides from tree to tree | To add sugar to something | *The sweet food made into grains, dissolved into syrup | A fond name, like honey
